.TH RUNRECEIPT 1
.SH NAME
runreceipt \- record local process and pipeline completion evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runreceipt
--label NAME [--execute --receipt NEWFILE] -- COMMAND [ARGUMENTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defaults to a JSON preview without execution. Explicit execution saves a private
intent record before starting and a final record with every stage's exit status.
Use --pipeline FILE for a JSON array of argv arrays. No shell expansion or retry
is performed. Output is forwarded unchanged; receipts omit output and raw arguments.
Argument fingerprints are not encryption and may reveal guessable arguments.
.SH LIMITS
A running receipt means completion is unknown. Local exit zero does not establish
remote success. Timeouts stop direct children; descendant or remote work may remain.
Store receipts in a private directory. Labels, executable paths and directories
are retained and should not contain secrets.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 all stages exited zero; 1 at least one failed; 2 usage; 4 recording or incomplete
execution; 124 timeout; 130 interrupt.
.SH SEE ALSO
rcdo receipt-review, ROADMAP.md
